<!--Post: 6211--><!--Time: 1107583619-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6211"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 10:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Perhaps my thinking is way too simplistic; however, I wondered if  BTK works &#40;or had worked&#41; in a slaughterhouse or meat packing plant.   <BR> <BR>Regardless of  whatever humane methods are now used, I would think that you have to be a very hardened person to stomach that occupation.    <BR> <BR>As a child, I knew an adult that worked in a slaughterhouse.  Even before I learned of his occupation, I somehow knew &#40;intuitively&#41; there was something odd about him.   <BR> <BR>Are/were there any of these slaughterhouses in the area?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6211-->
<!--Post: 6216--><!--Time: 1107588652-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6216"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 11:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://www.excelmeats.com/about/history.htm" target=_top>http://www.excelmeats.com/about/history.htm</a> <BR> <BR>This is cattle company...and we don&#39;t grow them for their fur.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6216-->
<!--Post: 6217--><!--Time: 1107589972-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6217"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 11:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Why not. He had to be employed somewhere in Wichita unless he was collecting some kind of disability or on welfare during the murders. <BR>It would explain being used to being in a death enviornment and a certain desensitivity to it. <BR>I would think that occupation may lead to someone being a knife or hatchet murderer more so than a strangler-suffocator. <BR>If Kathryn Bright is a BTK murder he did use a knife on her but wasn&#39;t very efficient with it. He stabbed her three times yet she was still alive when rescue arrived.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6217-->
<!--Post: 6219--><!--Time: 1107592391-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6219"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 12:33 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I am beginning to have doubts that BTK has any ACTUAL military training, and combat experience is even less likely. As you just pointed out, when he was rushed by the noise of the gun shots possibly alerting the neighbors, he had to rush. He stabbed Kathryn three times &#40;not killing her&#41; after shooting Kevin twice &#40;not killing him&#41;. One report even said that there were 5 casings found which would mean that he missed 3 times at point blank range. <BR> <BR>Something else I find VERY questionable is that an ex-military or ex-cop would use a 22 cal single action revolver.  <BR> <BR>I was thinking, at first, that he might pick a small &#40;tiny&#41; gun to reduce noise, but a revolver is a lot louder than an automatic, or that he planned to use it &#39;execution style&#39; like a hit man&#40;one bullet behind the ear, no blood or head parts&#41; but he seems to be fixed on strangulation as his first choice, and apparently the gun is his last.   <BR> <BR>He probably shot Kevin only because he was holding a gun at the time of the struggle. The gun is apparently for show &#40;and a really poor choice even for that&#41;. I bet when he&#39;s caught he has a wussy knife too.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6219-->
<!--Post: 6230--><!--Time: 1107615953-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6230"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 7:05 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Johno, <BR> <BR>Very good point, BTK didn&#39;t seem terribly &#34;knife- efficient&#34; in the Bright murder.   <BR> <BR>I&#39;ve read cases where stabbings took place and the knife would actually break against the victim&#39;s ribs.  But I believe these killings were spur-of-the-moment rage killings where somebody grabs a handy-dandy kitchen or utility knife and thinks they are going to fully penetrate the human torso. <BR> <BR>Do we know which part of the body Kathryn was stabbed in, and do we have any parameters on the knife &#40;via knife wounds&#41;? <BR> <BR>I guess one would have to know where to stab to get quick death, and where to get slow death. <BR> <BR>I&#39;m certainly no expert, but I&#39;m guessing he probably used a hunting knife or the like. <BR> <BR>But strangling is probably his specialty -- bloody messes are not.  Blood can be tracked all over the darn place.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6230-->
<!--Post: 6232--><!--Time: 1107617106-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6232"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 7:25 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Too messy for BTK. My father told me that years ago people who were employed in slaughter houses were not called for jury duty. That cannot be done today. There are no humane methods employed today in slaughter houses. Have you seen the bruising on turkeys and chickens? That only occurs while alive. BTK likes human prey. <BR> <BR>I wonder if he stabbed Ms. Bright from behind, thereby avoiding most of the blood splatter? I believe that he had to do a quick kill on her since things went wrong and he did not have the time to &#39;linger&#39;. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6232-->
<!--Post: 6236--><!--Time: 1107625308-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6236"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Blade<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Blade<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 9:41 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->A 22 caliber gun is used in a slaughter house for the killing of livestock.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6236-->
<!--Post: 6238--><!--Time: 1107625653-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6238"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jrl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 9:47 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Actually, a type of stun gun method is used, then their throat is slit.  A bullet a cow gets pretty expensive. <BR>I quote, &#34;What happens is that the animals go in single file. At a certain point, they pass over a bar, their legs on both sides, and the floor slowly drops away, and at that point they&#39;re being carried along sort of on that bar, which is a conveyor belt, and they then pass through a station where there&#39;s a man on the catwalk above. He&#39;s holding an object that looks like a power nailing gun or something. It&#39;s a pneumatic device called a stunner. <BR> <BR>This essentially injects a metal bolt. It&#39;s about the size and length of a thick pencil into its brain, right between the eyes, and that should render the animal brain dead. <BR> <BR>At that point, chains will be attached to his rear legs. He will be lifted up by the chains. The chains are attached to an overhead trolley, and then he will be bled. Another person in another station will stick a long knife in and cut his aorta and bleed the animal. And then he will be completely dead.&#34; <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6238-->
<!--Post: 6246--><!--Time: 1107630807-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6246"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 11:13 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Jrl: <BR> <BR>Simply disgusting.   <BR> <BR>It would just make me a quivering mass of jelly, and I would be so sick to see or hear these animals frightenend as they go in. <BR> <BR>I&#39;m sorry, but you have to be certain type of person to do this. <BR> <BR>Bmodule: <BR> <BR>Is that slaughterhouse you linked above anywhere near the killings?  How long has it been there? <BR> <BR>Our &#34;slaugherhouse discussion&#34; may seem terribly simplistic; however sometimes you just have to look at &#40;and accept&#41; the obvious.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6246-->
<!--Post: 6262--><!--Time: 1107642566-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6262"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Affie4u<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Affie4u<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 2:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Are there lots of meat packing/slaughterhouses <BR>in the Witicha area?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6262-->
<!--Post: 6315--><!--Time: 1107676434-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6315"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 11:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yes. When I typed &#39;Cattle Company&#39;, I meant Cattle Country. Wichita got it&#39;s start as a major rail hub for cattle drives.  <BR> <BR>Packing plants are still a major business. There is also a lot of hunting &#40;game dressing&#41; and farms with little old ladies who will go out to the yard, grab a chicken, wring it&#39;s neck and fix it for supper. My point being: there is no shortage of people who can stomach blood in the area. <BR> <BR>I still contend, however, that BTK is putting a lot of planning and effort into obtaining the opportunity of strangling his target slowly. He also writes in his letters of strangling some twice, bringing them close to death and allowing them to revive, then strangling them again. Read BTK&#39;s description under &#34;LETTERS&#34; on &#34;HOME&#34; page, referring to the Oteros &#40;it is disturbing&#41;. It explains how he derives a sexual release while strangling the victim.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6315-->
<!--Post: 6321--><!--Time: 1107684926-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6321"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Purple<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Purple<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 06, 2005 - 2:15 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Excel, also know as MBPXL, was located in two places.  Excel, the kill floor described above, was on 21st street and Mosley.  MBPXL, where the carcasses were transported to for processing was on 29th and Mead.  They quit processing at the 29th street location in the early 80&#39;s.  The kill floor was used for a short time after and then closed.  The building on 29th is still owned by Cargill, owner of Excel, and is in use.  The building on 21st is for sale.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6321-->
<!--Post: 6379--><!--Time: 1107739355-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6379"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Affie4u<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Affie4u<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 06, 2005 - 5:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I read BTK &#34;Letters&#34; B. It is Disturbing.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6379-->
<!--Post: 6485--><!--Time: 1107820986-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6485"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 07, 2005 - 4:03 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Iceteajan, Bright was stabbed three times in the abdomen. As for the knife size I don&#39;t know but I believe it was not a knife that her killer had with him but rather was her own knife that he took from her kitchen while rummaging through the house after having both Kathryn and her brother Kevin tied up.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6485-->
<!--Post: 6500--><!--Time: 1107833231-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6500"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 07, 2005 - 7:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I wonder if any of these slaughterhouses closed up &#40;or downsized&#41; around the time BTK resurfaced? <BR> <BR>Sorry - I&#39;m not from the area. <BR> <BR>I strongly believe that BTK has had a menial job in the Wichita area for some time.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6500-->
<!--Post: 6723--><!--Time: 1107982869-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6723"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 1:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->At 21st and Broadway the old slaughterhouse was called Cudahy&#39;s. Closed in the 70&#39;s and some of the employees were hired by Excel or Dold.  <BR>-Deb<!--/Text--></td></tr>
